1
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:06,240
In the lead,
the left-side competition

2
00:00:08,242 --> 00:00:09,842
(Penny:)Wow, you're really
good at this.

3
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:12,320
(Amy:)Well, I have an extremely
low center of gravity.

4
00:00:13,247 --> 00:00:14,747
(Amy:)I'm like a pyramid.

5
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:20,399
(Penny:)How you doing over there?

6
00:00:20,521 --> 00:00:22,591
(Leonard:)Oh, I hope it's just a sprain.

7
00:00:23,991 --> 00:00:25,701
(Leonard:)I cannot walk into that ER

8
00:00:25,726 --> 00:00:27,536
(Leonard:)with another video game injury.

9
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:31,439
(Penny:)Hey, Sheldon,
you want to play next?

10
00:00:31,565 --> 00:00:34,045
(Sheldon:)Oh, I would,
but I'm on my way out.

11
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:35,707
(Leonard:)-Where?
-Texas.

12
00:00:37,404 --> 00:00:39,444
(Amy:)Right now? Why?

13
00:00:39,606 --> 00:00:41,016
(Leonard:)-Is someone sick?
-Yes.

14
00:00:41,108 --> 00:00:44,278
(Sheldon:)My sister's uterus came
down with a baby.

15
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:47,452
(Penny:)Oh, she's pregnant?
That's great.

16
00:00:47,581 --> 00:00:49,421
(Penny:)You're gone an uncle--
Uncle Sheldon.

17
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:51,960
(Sheldon:)No, I will be Uncle Dr. Cooper.

18
00:00:53,186 --> 00:00:55,136
(Amy:)How come you never said
she was pregnant?

19
00:00:55,289 --> 00:00:57,129
(Sheldon:)Well, I never told you
about my brother's kidney stone.

20
00:00:57,291 --> 00:00:58,391
(Sheldon:)You want to hear about everything

21
00:00:58,525 --> 00:01:00,235
(Sheldon:)that comes out
of my family's genitals?

22
00:01:01,595 --> 00:01:03,045
(Leonard:)Well, congrats, and it's nice

23
00:01:03,130 --> 00:01:04,470
(Leonard:)you're gonna be
there for your sister.

24
00:01:04,598 --> 00:01:07,208
(Sheldon:)Yes. I'm filling in for her
husband who's recovering

25
00:01:07,301 --> 00:01:09,471
(Sheldon:)from a horrible motorcycle accident.

26
00:01:09,636 --> 00:01:11,746
(Sheldon:)Lucky duck.

27
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:14,546
(Penny:)Wow, so, how long will you be gone?

28
00:01:14,641 --> 00:01:16,311
(Sheldon:)Well, she's due tomorrow.

29
00:01:16,476 --> 00:01:18,456
(Sheldon:)Although it did take her
six years to finish high school,

30
00:01:18,579 --> 00:01:19,889
(Sheldon:)so who knows?

31
00:01:20,581 --> 00:01:22,121
(Amy:)Can I give you a ride to the airport?

32
00:01:22,249 --> 00:01:24,819
(Sheldon:)Oh, no, thank you, I don't want
to be an inconvenience.

33
00:01:25,619 --> 00:01:30,019
(Sheldon:)Chop-chop, Leonard.
We leave in ten minutes.

